# Trivy Security Scan Suppressions
# CVE-2023-28155: Server-Side Request Forgery in Request Package
# Risk Assessment: LOW RISK
#
# Context:
# - The 'request' package (v2.88.2) is used by matrix-bot-sdk for HTTP requests to Matrix homeservers
# - Matrix homeservers are trusted infrastructure components
# - The bot only connects to pre-configured, trusted Matrix servers
# - No user-controlled URLs are passed to the request library
# - The SSRF vulnerability requires attacker control of request URLs, which is not possible in this deployment
#
# Mitigation:
# - Matrix homeserver URLs are configured in infrastructure (not user-controlled)
# - All Matrix traffic uses HTTPS with certificate validation
# - Bot runs in isolated container with network restrictions
#
# TODO: Migrate matrix-admin-bot to use matrix-js-sdk directly or a modern Matrix bot SDK
# that doesn't depend on the deprecated 'request' package.
#
# Suppression expires: 2027-04-21 (1 year from issue creation)
CVE-2023-28155